From: Polaris Lab <polaris@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: polaris: select host for a controlled USB test

The current board DT fixes DWC3 in peripheral mode. Wi-Fi SSH and encrypted
Wi-Fi credentials now work across reboot, allowing an independent host-data
path test without relying on the USB gadget for access.

Use a separate diagnostic boot image to select host mode. This changes no
PMIC registers, charger configuration, Type-C policy, or VBUS regulator. It
does not implement automatic role switching or claim working bus power.
Keep the LCD/touch/Wi-Fi test02 image as the immediate rollback.

Signed-off-by: Polaris Lab <polaris@localhost>

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-polaris.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-polaris.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-polaris.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-polaris.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-polaris.dts
@@ -644,7 +644,7 @@ &usb_1 {
 };
 
 &usb_1_dwc3 {
-	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+	dr_mode = "host";
 
 	/* Fastest mode for USB 2 */
 	maximum-speed = "high-speed";
